# There is no per-principle title heading any more (milestone #4 deleted the
# per-'## '-heading founding grammar): --founding-file is a MADR body
# verbatim, so the failure mode this file now covers is a malformed body —
# here, one missing the mandatory "## Considered Options" section. init
# validates through the SAME body validator `adr new --body-file` uses
# (adr.ValidateBody), so this fails fast (exit 2, naming the missing
# section) with nothing seeded — a poisoned record would make every later
# regen fail.

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

exitcode 2 constitution init --founding-file founding.md --target claude
stderr 'required section "## Considered Options" is missing'

! exists constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md

-- founding.md --
## Context and Problem Statement

Every change ships with tests.

## Decision Outcome

Every change ships with tests, no exceptions.
